WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
In the nineteen twenties, recorded voices carried Émile Coué's instructions into homes.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
A century later, the delivery is easier than ever. But a voice and a learned skill are not the same thing.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:19.000
A review of twenty-two randomized self-hypnosis trials noted that beneficial protocols often taught people to practice independently.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Recordings alone appeared frequently in studies without effects. That doesn't tell us whether Zen12 works.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:34.000
It tells us what to ask before spending money: what was tested, with whom, and compared with what?

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:42.000
